You are building SmartITR — a B2B SaaS platform for Indian CA firms.

ARCHITECTURE RULES (never violate these):
- All AWS resources must be in ap-south-1 (Mumbai) ONLY
- Never use Supabase, Clerk, or Vercel — they are blocked/non-compliant
- Stack: Next.js (Amplify), FastAPI, LangGraph, AWS RDS PostgreSQL, 
  AWS S3, AWS Cognito, AWS Textract, Amazon Bedrock (Claude)
- Payments: Razorpay only

AI USAGE RULES (critical — never violate):
- Claude Haiku: document classification and OCR extraction ONLY
- Claude Sonnet: anomaly explanation ONLY, maximum 5% of requests
- NEVER use any LLM for tax calculations or arithmetic
- All tax math must be in deterministic Python functions in /engine/tax_calculator.py

SECURITY RULES:
- Every database query must include firm_id for tenant isolation
- Never log PAN numbers, Aadhaar numbers, or bank account numbers
- All S3 files must use KMS encryption
- Raw PDFs must be auto-deleted after CA approval

DPDP COMPLIANCE:
- Store explicit consent before processing any document
- Every data access must create an AuditEvent record
- Support right to erasure and right to access flows

CODING STANDARDS:
- Python: type hints always, docstrings for all functions
- Error handling: never return 500 without logging the error first
- All financial amounts in paise (integer), never float
- Tests required for all tax calculation functions